SubClassOf(<https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/IndicationProcess> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasSpecifiedOutput> <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/VisualIndication>))

# Class: <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000127> (indicator)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000127> "indicator"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/annotation/naturalLanguageDefinition> <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000127> "An indicator is an instrument that displays or shows the value or status of a measured variable or condition to make it perceptible to operators."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/annotation/naturalLanguageDefinition> <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000127> "Um indicador é um instrumento que exibe ou mostra o valor ou status de uma variável medida ou condição para torná-la perceptível aos operadores."@pt-br)
AnnotationAssertion(<https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/annotation/semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom> <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000127> "Every indicator is an instrument that bears an indication function to display process information in human-perceptible form."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/annotation/firstOrderLogicAxiom> <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000127> "∀x(Indicator(x) ↔ (Instrument(x) ∧ ∃f(IndicationFunction(f) ∧ bearerOf(x,f))))"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000127> "[ISO 15926-4] An <INDICATOR> is an <INSTRUMENTATION FUNCTION> that has a capability of <INDICATING>"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000127> "[SLB Glossary] A visible sign of a chemical reaction."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000127> "[OnePetro] In a chemical context, an indicator is a chemical in a titration reaction that changes color at a certain pH.\n        \n        In the context of a mechanical load, an indicator is a dial or gauge."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000127> "[POSC Caesar] An artefact that is a intended to display the value or the status of a condition."@en)
EquivalentClasses(<https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000127> ObjectIntersectionOf(<https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000091> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasFunction> <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/IndicationFunction>)))
DisjointClasses(<https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000127> <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000157>)
DisjointClasses(<https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000127> <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000234>)
DisjointClasses(<https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000127> <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000207>)

