# Class: <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000245> (densitometer)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000245> "densitometer"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/annotation/naturalLanguageDefinition> <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000245> "A densitometer is an instrument that bears a density measurement function."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/annotation/naturalLanguageDefinition> <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000245> "Um densitômetro é um instrumento que possui uma função de medição de densidade."@pt-br)
AnnotationAssertion(<https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/annotation/semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom> <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000245> "Every densitometer is an instrument that has the function of measuring density."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/annotation/firstOrderLogicAxiom> <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000245> "∀x(Densitometer(x) ↔ Instrument(x) ∧ ∃f(DensityMeasurementFunction(f) ∧ bearerOf(x,f)))"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000245> "[ISO 15926-4] A <DENSITOMETER> is an <INSTRUMENTATION ITEM> and a <MEASURING INSTRUMENT> that measures the degree of darkness in photographic or semitransparent material. The densitometer is basically a light source aimed at a photoelectric cell which determines the density of the sample from differences in the readings"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000245> "[SLB Glossary] A device installed on a mixing or pumping system manifold to measure the density of fluids."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000245> "[OnePetro] A device used for reading the density of a flowing fluid or slurry."@en)
