# Class: <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000316> (nozzle)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000316> "nozzle"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/annotation/naturalLanguageDefinition> <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000316> "A nozzle is a material artifact that has a protruding part with a shaped orifice designed to direct fluid flow into a specific pattern."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/annotation/naturalLanguageDefinition> <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000316> "Um bocal é um artefato material que possui uma parte protuberante com um orifício moldado projetado para direcionar o fluxo de fluido em um padrão específico."@pt-br)
AnnotationAssertion(<https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/annotation/semiFormalNaturalLanguageAxiom> <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000316> "Every nozzle is a material artifact that bears a fluid direction function and has a shaped orifice and protruding part as component parts."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/annotation/firstOrderLogicAxiom> <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000316> "∀x(Nozzle(x) ↔ MaterialArtifact(x) ∧ ∃f(FluidDirectionFunction(f) ∧ bearerOf(x,f)) ∧ ∃o(ShapedOrifice(o) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,o)) ∧ ∃p(ProtrudingPart(p) ∧ hasComponentPartAtAllTimes(x,p)))"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000316> "[ISO 15926-4] A <NOZZLE> is an <ARTEFACT> and a <FLUID PORT> and a <CONNECTOR> that is a protruding part through which a stream of fluid is directed"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000316> "[CFIHOS] A physical object that has a protruding part through which a stream of fluid is directed."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000316> "[DEXPI] A projecting short piece of pipe that is attached to another (hollow) body."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000316> "[OnePetro] A shaped orifice for directing fluid flow."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(skos:definition <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000316> "[POSC Caesar] A physical object that has a protruding part through which a stream of fluid is directed."@en)
EquivalentClasses(<https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000316> ObjectIntersectionOf(<https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/MaterialArtifact> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/hasFunction> <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/FluidDirectionFunction>)))
DisjointClasses(<https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000316> <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/COPI_0000077>)

# Class: <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/PowerTransmissionFunction> (power transmission function)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/PowerTransmissionFunction> "power transmission function"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/annotation/naturalLanguageDefinition> <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/PowerTransmissionFunction> "A Shaft that participates in mechanical energy output processes, serving as the exit point for mechanical energy transmission from a prime mover to external energy consuming equipment."@en)
SubClassOf(<https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/PowerTransmissionFunction> <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/construct/DesignedFunction>)
SubClassOf(<https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/PowerTransmissionFunction> ObjectAllValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000054> <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/PowerTransmissionProcess>))
SubClassOf(<https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/PowerTransmissionFunction> ObjectSomeValuesFrom(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000054> <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/PowerTransmissionProcess>))

# Class: <https://www.inf.ufrgs.br/ontologies/copi/PowerTransmissionProcess> (power transmission process)

